 "notes": "Single nutrients folded into t types on Vitamin supplement and Mineral supplement (old Vitamin D, Vitamin C, Magnesium kinds merged). Cut retail SKU noise from the old Walgreens harvest: DEVA, GNC, Garden of Life, InnovixLabs, Piping Rock, USANA, Health Thru Nutrition and duplicate Carlson D3 lines, plus One A Day Men's, Mag-Ox and Nature's Bounty Essential Prenatal Gummies to stay within 12 models, and 'Centrum (men's multivitamin)' and 'One A Day (women's multivitamin)' which were vague. Kept prenatal/children's as Multivitamin types (not split out, so no baby tag). Kirkland Signature left out: no product or brand page retrieved. Holland & Barrett and Solgar are in the register but have no models because no product names were retrieved. ConsumerLab and USP lists are paywalled/not retrieved; Healthline's tested brand review (Thorne best overall) used as the independent test source."
